    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald is delighted to present No. 19 Fairhaven Close to the market for sale. This fabulous 3 storey, semi-detached home is situated in one of Castleknock's most sought-after developments, just a stone's throw from the magnificent Phoenix Park. Built in 2018 by the highly regarded Flynn O'Flaherty, No. 19 is one of only 4 of its kind within Fairhaven. Thoughtfully designed and finished to an excellent standard throughout, the property combines contemporary style with generous living accommodation and superb storage space.\n\nExtending to approximately 156 sq.m./1680 sq.ft., this property offers expansive living space which is in excellent condition. At ground floor level is the bright and welcoming entrance hallway with paneled walls, which flows through to the guest WC. To the right is the tastefully decorated living room, with a feature solid fuel stove and double doors leading out to the open-plan kitchen/dining/reception room. The first floor hosts 3 generous bedrooms, all with fitted wardrobes. One of the double bedrooms to rear benefits from having a second ensuite bathroom. The contemporary family bathroom completes this floor. Occupying the entire second floor is the incredibly impressive, primary bedroom which boasts a luxurious, walk-in wardrobe as well as an ensuite. There is a large storage room, as well as having ample storage space in the eaves. \n\nTo the front of this fantastic semi-detached home is a cobblelock driveway to fit 2 cars. A gated side entrance leads to the south/east facing rear garden, which is mainly lawned with a separate, paved patio area. A timber shed provides convenient outdoor storage. \n\nAs well as being just a stone's throw from the Phoenix Park, Fairhaven is a short stroll to Castleknock Village and all of its amenities. The Phoenix Park Racecourse, next to Fairhaven, holds a 'Londis' convenience store, café and a pharmacy. There are a number of both primary and secondary schools nearby, including St Brigids National School, Castleknock Educate Together, Edmund Rice Secondary School, Castleknock College and Mount Sackville (school admission policies are subject to change and should be verified). Ashtown Train Station is less than a 10 minute walk, with Broombridge LUAS line just 2 stops away, as well as having an excellent bus service to City Centre, on the Navan Road. There is also immediate access to the N3, M3 and M50, as well as Dublin Airport being just a 20 minute drive approx.\n\nViewing is highly recommended to appreciate the quality, space, and superb setting of this wonderful family home."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHallway - \nAccessed through a high-quality front door, the hallway has tiled flooring, with beautiful, paneled walls. Has convenient under-stair, push storage and a separate press which is plumbed for a washing machine.\n\nGuest WC - \nWith tiled flooring and paneled walls continuing from the hallway. Comprises of a WC and wash hand basin, with stylish, chrome finishes.\n\nLiving Room - \nA tastefully decorated, well-proportioned living room with laminate timber flooring and contemporary, paneled walls. A solid fuel stove provides a lovely, homely feature to the room. Double doors provide access to the wonderful, open-plan kitchen/dining/reception room.\n\nKitchen/Dining/Reception Room - \nA fabulous, open-plan room, with tiled flooring and striking, feature light fitting. The contemporary-style kitchen, designed by Nolans kitchens, is fitted with an integrated oven, gas hob, fridge/freezer and dishwasher. Double doors provide access to the rear garden.\n\nLanding - \nWith laminate timber flooring and paneled walls, continuing from the downstairs hallway. Holds the hotpress.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nA very spacious, double bedroom with laminate timber flooring and fitted wardrobes, overlooking the rear garden.\n\nEnsuite - \nA second ensuite bathroom, with tiled flooring and partly tiled walls. Comprises of a WC, wash hand basin and a shower. A fitted vanity cabinet completes.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nA third, double bedroom with laminate timber flooring and fitted wardrobes, located to the front of the house.\n\nBedroom 4 - \nA generous, single bedroom with laminate timber flooring and fitted wardrobe.\n\nBathroom - \nFully tiled, contemporary-style family bathroom comprises of a WC, wash hand basin and a shower over the bath. An LED mirror and fitted storage press complete.\n\n2nd Floor Landing - \nWith laminate timber flooring and paneled walls continuing from the first floor. Holds a large storage room.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nAn incredibly impressive primary suite, spanning the entire second floor of the house. Finished with laminate timber flooring, this expansive room boasts a large window, as well as overhead skylights, which flood the room with natural light. There is excellent storage space, with a luxurious, walk-in wardrobe as well as substantial storage in the eaves. There is also a built-in dressing table/desk to the side of the room.\n\nEnsuite - \nWith tiled flooring and partly tiled walls, the ensuite consists of a WC, wash hand basin and a shower. An LED fitted mirror completes.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>'A' rated home built in 2018</li><li>Tado Smart Water Heating System with Smart Thermostats on all radiators.</li><li>3 x Reolink security cameras (rear, side, front) connected to a digital recorder.</li><li>Ethernet Cat5 network cable throughout the house.</li><li>Expansive living space, over 3 floors</li><li>4 bathrooms, to include 2 ensuites</li><li>Solar thermal panels</li><li>South/east facing garden to rear</li><li>Minutes' walk from the Phoenix Park</li><li>Excellent local amenities & transport links</ul>"
      },
